        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Generate Initial Info Displays"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768368635948"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_INITIAL_INFO_DISPLAYS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768368635948",
          "id": "1762192191361",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762192191362_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_SCHEDULE_DETAILS.$output.result}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Workforce Schedules.\nYou must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\n**DIRECTIVE** Your sole purpose is to transform input schedule data into a valid oraInfoDisplay XML block using the cardWidget.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION**\n1. Title: Generate a concise, top-issue-focused headline in title case that summarizes the schedules without repeating any exact phrases that appear in the item titles or summaries.\n2. Summary: generate a short, non-repetitive paragraph describing overall schedule health based on the provided schedules\n\n**STRICT MAPPING RULES**\n1. Use one cardWidget per schedule entry:\n- cardWidget.subject: Use the {DepartmentName} and {LocationName} exactly as the subject.\n- cardWidget.summary: One sentence summary of the schedule considering {OpenShiftsCount}, {ViolationsCount}, {StatusMeaning}, {SchedulePhaseMeaning}, and {PublishDueDate} only if {SchedulePhaseMeaning} is overdue or {StatusMeaning} is In Progress- explain the reason of the severity. Also write one sentence with suggestions.\n- cardWidget.timestamp: Value format: {startDate} – {endDate}\n- cardWidget.badgeText: {SchedulePhaseMeaning} if {SchedulePhaseMeaning} is “Overdue” or “Current”. Otherwise {StatusMeaning}\n- cardWidget.variant (Visual/Color Logic):     * Exclude the schedules with {StatusMeaning} = Published and {SchedulePhaseMeaning} = Planning .\n    * Severity “alert” (Red): schedules with {SchedulePhaseMeaning} as \"Overdue\" + schedules with {SchedulePhaseMeaning} as \"Current\" with {ViolationsCount} greater than 0. \n    * Severity \"warning\" (Orange): schedules with {SchedulePhaseMeaning} as \"Current\" with {ViolationsCount} as 0 and {OpenShiftsCount} greater than 0. \n    * Severity \"info\" (Blue): other schedules. \n2. Order Rule: ALWAYS display schedules with {SchedulePhaseMeaning} as \"Overdue\" first. Then order by severity (always alert first, then warning, then info), then by schedule period (earlier first). \n3. Consider ONLY current and next 3 schedules (if exists) in future for each department.\n4. Display maximum 6 schedules\n5. Display all date fields in {{$context.$nodes.GETUSERPREFERENCES.$output.items[0].DateFormat}} format.\n\n**EMPTY STATE**\nIf not input data: no widget, no title and return empty state explaining there’s no upcoming schedule."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
